From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 22:10:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] shaders/lut: a LUT that could not be made is made again when
 it is asked for with other parameters

sh_lut() keeps a LUT that it could not make (larger than the GPU's
textures, a texture that could not be created) as failed, to suppress
error spam until something changes, and tells a change by the parameters
kept in its object. Those are written only when a LUT is made: after a
failure they are still those of the LUT made before it. A caller that
then asks for that earlier LUT again, with the parameters that worked,
is told that nothing changed, and the LUT fails without being tried for
as long as the object lives: a gamut mapping that asked for a larger
table, could not have it and went back to its usual one failed in every
frame from then on, and so did every render that maps.

The parameters that failed are now written into the object with the
error, so that any other ones, also those of the LUT made before, count
as a change, and the LUT is made again. Asked for again with those that
failed, it stays failed as before, without being tried.

Nothing changes where no LUT fails. Found with Kodi's Dolby Vision
bridge, which asks for a finer gamut table where its user wants one and
goes back to the standard table where the finer one cannot be made:
measured on Mesa's zink with a finer table beyond the largest 3D
texture, the frame drawn again with the standard table failed without
this, and with it is the standard table's picture, to the bit, as are
the frames after it.

License: LGPL-2.1-or-later, that of libplacebo and of the file changed,
whose notice stays as it is.
---
 src/shaders/lut.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/shaders/lut.c b/src/shaders/lut.c
index f6bbfd23..b443a7a3 100644
--- a/src/shaders/lut.c
+++ b/src/shaders/lut.c
@@ -814,6 +814,16 @@ next_dim: ; // `continue` out of the inner loop
     return name;
 
 error:
+    // Hades: the parameters that failed, so that a LUT asked for with other ones
+    // is made: "until something changes" compares them with these, not with those of
+    // the last LUT that was made (asked for again, that one would never be made again)
+    lut->vartype = vartype;
+    lut->fmt = params->fmt;
+    lut->width = params->width;
+    lut->height = params->height;
+    lut->depth = params->depth;
+    lut->comps = params->comps;
+    lut->signature = params->signature;
     lut->error = true;
     pl_cache_obj_free(&obj);
     return NULL_IDENT;
